Tally is an old [[Phenomena/Hearts|Heart]] deep in the lower hull of the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence|Providence]], and the town that has grown up around it. The heart is warm and cased in a metal shell, and buildings have been raised in the heat that comes off it. It was the strider's timekeeper: it kept the religious rites, logged what the strider did and where it went, and kept it moving smoothly forward. The [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence/Machine God|Machine God]] said it was already dead, and so it is: the heart is cold, its veins still.

The town around the heart is Neweth, old and buried in the strider. Its people, one to two thousand of them, are [[Bestiary/Mongrel Folk|mongrel folk]] and other outcasts indentured to the strider's owners. They trade in ration slips instead of coin and have built a working, somewhat violent civilization in the dark. They are unlikely to attack strangers on sight, though what they make of people outside their class is hard to guess.

[[People/Galzu|Galzu]], [[People/Anzu|Anzu]]'s sister, was working to revive the dead Heart from the inner sanctum above it, calling it back to life with a slow ritual. The remaining followers of [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Herald|Herald]] on the strider, called the Herald's Children, keep near the heart and pass for townsfolk, and people of the [[Org/Iridescent Church/index|Iridescent Church]] have gone underground almost directly above it.
